course: dictionary
lesson: 5299
title: Justly: fair and rightly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Justly is an adverb. It tells you how something is done. It means fairly, in a way that is right and treats people equally. «Treat people justly» means treat everyone fairly, without favouring one person.
explain: Justly can also mean rightly, with good reason. «Justly proud» means proud for a good reason, because you earned it. «Justly punished» means punished in a way that is deserved.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Ask: is the sentence about fairness, or about something deserved? In «a ruler governs while he rules justly», the words around it, such as governs and disasters, show that the topic is fair rule. Then swap in fairly or rightly and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Justly is an adverb, and it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Justly» means fairly, treating people equally.
fact: «Justly» also means rightly, with good reason, as in «justly proud».
fact: The Zhou dynasty (1046–256 BC) taught that a ruler who did not rule «justly» could lose the right to rule.
fact: A good check is to swap in fairly or rightly and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The judge treated everyone justly, so no one was punished unfairly.» What does justly mean? | *Fairly, treating people equally | Quickly and loudly | Hidden under a cloak | Angrily, with a shout
exercise: «She was justly proud of her science project, which she had worked on for months.» What does justly mean here? | Secretly, in a whisper | *Rightly, with good reason | Sadly and slowly | Wrongly, with no reason
exercise: In «a ruler governs while he rules justly», which word is the adverb? | while | governs | ruler | *justly
test: «The thief was justly punished by the court.» Why is justly a good word here? | It shows the court was closed | It shows the thief was very tall | *It shows the punishment was fair and deserved | It shows the thief was caught by chance
test: The Zhou idea was that a ruler must govern justly. What does justly show about how he should rule? | Quickly, so the work is finished soon | Secretly, so no one knows the plan | Loudly, so everyone can hear him | *Fairly and rightly, so people are treated equally
exam: «Ana was justly famous for her kind, fair work, and everyone agreed she deserved it.» What does justly suggest? | Only sometimes, now and then | *Rightly, because she deserved her fame | Quietly, in a whisper | Wrongly, with no reason at all
